## How to use the forum

+ For each question, write a short and specific subject line that makes it clear exactly what you’re talking about.
+ Before seeking basic information, please check manuals, websites and similar resources. Questions that spark a discussion, on the other hand, are always welcome.
+ Even though the post with which you start a discussion is called a ‘question’, you can post a comment on a relevant topic. In this case, it is implied: ‘What do you think?’.
+ Before posting an answer, read the entire thread and avoid one-line answers.
+ If you wish to introduce a different topic, start with a new question.
+ Other participants want to discuss things with you: therefore, do not use artificial intelligence tools for your posts.
+ Avoid posting private information about yourself or other people.
+ Write in a manner that is respectful towards everyone and ignore posts that are not.
+ Before posting, check that your message is clear and free of errors. Once you’ve pressed the ‘Publish’ button, you won’t be able to edit it.
+ Don’t expect participants to read and reply immediately: written discussions encourage more reflection.

## How to use RSS feeds

To stay up to date with new messages, you can use an RSS reader. Here are a few to choose from:

+ Android: [FeedFlow](https://play.google.com/store/search?q=FeedFlow&c=apps) ([F-Droid](https://f-droid.org/packages/com.prof18.feedflow/)), [Feeder](https://play.google.com/store/search?q=Feeder&c=apps) ([F-Droid](https://f-droid.org/en/packages/com.nononsenseapps.feeder/)), [RSS Reader](https://f-droid.org/en/packages/de.lolo.rssreader/), [Aggregator News](https://play.google.com/store/search?q=Aggregator%20News&c=apps)
+ Linux: [Liferea](https://github.com/lwindolf/liferea), [GFeeds](https://gfeeds.gabmus.org/), [Akregator](https://apps.kde.org/akregator/)
+ iOS: [NetNewsWire](https://apps.apple.com/it/app/netnewswire-rss-reader/id1480640210)
+ MacOS: [NetNewsWire](https://netnewswire.com/)
+ Windows: [FeedFlow](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9n5t1rfbb6v5), [Fluent Reader](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/9p71fc94lrh8)

Install one and add the feed you want. Yellow Talk offers a general feed, which provides updates from all groups, and a specific feed for each group. You can use the aggregators’ auto-discovery feature.

## How to use Markdown

You can use some Markdown in your messages.

To format text:

```
Normal *italics* **bold**
```

To create paragraphs:

```
This is the first paragraph. The next paragraph must be separated by a blank line.

This is the second paragraph.
```

To create block quotes:

```
> This is a quote.
```

To create lists:

```
+ First item
+ Second item
+ Third item
```

To create links:

```
Link to a [website](https://example.org)
Link to an [image](https://example.org/image.jpg)
```

If an image is not available online, you can first upload it to a file-sharing service, such as [ImgBB](https://imgbb.com/).
